WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:04.330
10.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:05.330
9.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.330
8.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.830
7.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:16.790
(TOGETHER) 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.200
Howdy.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.780
We are back and ready for the next episode of Ghostwriter,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.160
Beyond the Page.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.040
Today we're going to dig in deeper

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.250
with one of my personal favorite books

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:31.520
because we are going to jump into the wild, wild west

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:37.383
of outer space with Trinity, written by yours truly, me.

00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:38.300
That's me right there.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.850
I really loved writing this book because it's

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.990
full of adventure, excitement, and twists and turns

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.910
as the two main characters, Hitch and Dale,

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:51.030
travel along a winding trail in search of the truth.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.100
So I'm really excited to see what winding road Ghostwriter

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.930
is going to put Donna on to get her

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.790
closer to finishing her story.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.460
Let's check it out.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.459
Welcome to Donna's Video Diary.

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:07.460
So far we have who, Sapphire the Spider.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.440
And now we have where.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.040
For my setting, I decided what better place for Sapphire

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.470
and her friends than a place we all know

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.470
is filled with amazing adventures, surprises,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.770
and information-- the bookstore.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:24.580
I think writing about a place I can really picture

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.870
is going to help me feel more sure of my descriptions.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.370
Plus, it's so cool to think about the bookstore

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.490
from Sapphire's tiny perspective.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.710
The fashion section is where she, of course,

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.540
spends most of her time.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.360
But she also goes to school in the textbook section

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.860
with her friends.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.540
And her older brother Spelman plays

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.250
soccer in the sports section.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.740
There's so many amazing places they can explore

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.090
right there in the store.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:52.390
Now, let's see what might be up next.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:53.375
Nothing?

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:55.750
I thought Ghostwriter would have shared something by now.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.880
Why.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.670
Ghostwriter is really sticking to a pattern with these hints.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.678
Let's see.

00:02:06.678 --> 00:02:07.178
Why?

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:13.290
Why, why, why?

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.743
Well, hello there, Miss Donna.

00:02:15.743 --> 00:02:17.160
What is it you're trying to solve?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.510
Dale!

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.262
I'm so glad you're here.

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:21.720
You always show up to save the day.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.610
Well, I'm flattered.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.330
Is there something you need help with, some kind of mission?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.920
You could say that.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.010
I really want to finish this mission,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.170
but I keep getting stuck.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.580
That is tricky.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.330
For me, when it comes to fighting crime and chasing down

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.582
scoundrels, it's certainly much harder

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:43.290
to come up with a resolution if you don't

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.570
know what the real problem is.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.760
When Hitch and I were after the Camarillo Kid,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.910
we didn't know what he was after, or where he was headed.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.540
But once we figured out he was after the Trinity,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.120
we had a much better chance of catching him.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.920
As we were trying to recover the Trinity,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.080
we ran into conflicts and obstacles

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.830
every step of the way, from an army of knights in armor

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.030
to a double-crossing mayor.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:07.530
Wow.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.800
What a story.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.010
It's like every moment builds on top of the one

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:15.860
before until everything finally gets fixed.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.685
Wait.

00:03:16.685 --> 00:03:18.530
Dale, that's perfect.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.660
You have no idea how much you just helped.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.070
You totally saved my day!

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.870
Very glad to hear it.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.900
I'll be on my way.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.370
Hitch is waiting at the station for me.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.660
Best of luck, Miss Donna.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.180
What Dale goes through in Trinity,

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.510
all of the ups and downs, the action moments,

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.540
and the resolution she finally comes to with Hitch,

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:46.370
those are all elements you need to create a plot of any story.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.780
I've so got it.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.850
This hint is all about plot.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.950
It's the whole reason why I've put together

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.560
my character and setting to actually put them

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.800
into the story.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.590
I bet there's a good chapter in Trinity

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.330
full of action-packed plot moments to help me out.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.910
Let's try chapter 8.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.950
At this point in the story, we already

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.470
know that the Rivins are a rebel colony living

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.450
on a planet called Tensor-4.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.080
And they're causing a lot more trouble than anyone realized.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.810
I can't wait to read how Dale uses her training as a sky

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.839
marshal to help her out.

00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:21.490
"Come out, come out," the bald Rivin

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.130
called to Dale in a singsong voice.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.620
"You don't want us to blow open the hatch, now, do you?"

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.270
Whoa.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:34.930
Dale's mind raced.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.220
She was scared.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.020
Really scared.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.180
"What do you want from me?" she called out.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.200
"From you?

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.720
Nothing at all," the Rivin called back.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.950
"You're free to go.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.130
We want your ship."

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.620
No, they couldn't get the ship.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.630
It would be better if it was destroyed.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.820
And Dale knew how.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.570
"OK!"

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:56.620
Dale called.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.180
"I'm coming out."

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.830
She had to work fast.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.230
If the Rivins suspected that something wasn't right,

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.720
they might blow up the ship.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.360
"Just getting my gear together," Dale yelled.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.160
All deputies were taught to be prepared

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.160
for situations like this one.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.170
It was a drastic move, but Dale saw no other way.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.080
She stood over the cockpit controls

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.690
and entered a series of special commands.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.150
Her fingers flew over the control console,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.150
inputting the commands in what she hoped was the exact right

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.930
order because she wouldn't be getting a second chance.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.120
There were 20 commands in all.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.640
When she reached the final one, she held her breath

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.920
and threw the last toggle switch.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.570
Instantly, every light on the cockpit panel flashed red.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.410
"Yes!"

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.240
Dale pumped her fist in victory.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.550
She'd done it.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.080
The ship was disabled.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.100
Forever.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.280
No command could make it ever fly again.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.920
From that moment on, the ship was about as useful

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.110
as a garbage dumpster.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.070
"Time's up!"

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.400
The Rivin was losing his patience.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.350
"OK, I'm coming out!"

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.390
Dale ran to the far side of the ship,

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:07.090
where her flight cycle, LuluBelle sat.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:10.050
She jumped into the saddle and powered up.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.280
LuluBelle rose a few inches off the deck.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.190
Dale punched a command into her wristband computer,

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:18.460
and the ship's hatch door began to rise.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.190
She gunned LuluBelle's engine and sped forward.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.040
She flew through the opening with barely an inch

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.110
overhead to spare.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.870
Dale shot away from the ship, past the group of surprised

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:32.830
Rivins, and into the night.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.050
That was amazing.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.500
This chapter is basically a whole story by itself

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.020
as Dale overcomes the trouble with the Rivins.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.270
It all makes so much sense now.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:46.960
A story is made up of the setup, or exposition,

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.360
the conflict with all of its obstacles,

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.520
and finally, the resolution.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.380
Let's dive right in.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.350
Donna is in great shape.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.660
She's been working really hard, and she has come up

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.520
with her characters.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.450
She's come up with her setting.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.470
And now she's working out all the interesting key plot

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.150
points for her story.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.320
And I hope you are, too.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.300
You're still working on your story, right?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.070
And you're still writing those ideas down

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:19.460
in your bullet journal, because there's no better way

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.265
to brainstorm ideas than writing it down in your journal.

00:07:22.265 --> 00:07:24.360
So I hope you're doing that.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.470
And if you want to dive deeper into the Ghostwriter world,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.500
be sure to pick up Trinity and read it.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.382
It's my book.

00:07:32.382 --> 00:07:33.840
And then go to the Wild, Wild Ghost

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.450
section of the activity guide.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.690
And as always, check in with the entire Ghostwriter gang

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.480
on Apple TV+ for episodes of the show.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.950
So until then, we'll see you.

